<title>UK: BAA passenger traffic up 4.6 pct in 96/97.</title>
<headline>BAA passenger traffic up 4.6 pct in 96/97.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airport operator BAA Plc said on Monday that passenger trafic at its seven UK airports rose 4.6 percent to 98 million in the financial year 1996/97.</p>
<p>Traffic rose 6.3 percent to 8.2 million in March compared with a year ago, BAA said.  </p>
<p>Cargo tonnage was up 5.7 percent at 1.5 million tonnes in the full 1996/97 year, while it rose by 8.0 percent to 138,914 in March.</p>
<p>Passenger traffic at London Heathrow increased by 3.5 percent in March to 4.8 million passengers and by 12.4 percent to 2.0 million passengers at London Gatwick.</p>
<p>BAA traffic statistics for March 1997 vs March 1996</p>
<p>Passengers (millions)</p>
<p>London Heathrow - 4.818 (up 3.5 pct)</p>
<p>London Gatwick -  1.998 (up 12.4 pct)</p>
<p>London Stansted - 0.391 (up 14.8 pct)</p>
<p>Glasgow - 0.407 (up 3.6 pct)</p>
<p>Edinburgh - 0.306 (up 5.3 pct)</p>
<p>Aberdeen - 0.196 (up 6.7 pct)</p>
<p>Southampton - 0.043 (up 10.7 pct)</p>
<p>Cargo (tonnes)</p>
<p>London Heathrow - 97,429 (up 5.7 pct)</p>
<p>London Gatwick - 27,542 up 13.2 pct)</p>
<p>London Stansted - 11,897 (up 23.0 pct)</p>
<p>Glasgow - 776 (down 35.2 pct)</p>
<p>Edinburgh - 687 (up 5.7 pct)</p>
<p>Aberdeen - 528 (up 3.7 pct)</p>
<p>Southampton - 55 (down 1.8 pct)</p>
